Add lean SFT commits (bit 20): header-word ACK, Rwrite-only custody

SOPHIA_SFT_LEAN_CAPABILITY (1 << 20) is an explicitly required r13 option on
top of terminal-only. A complete frame-submit FrameCommit carries the
cumulative ACK in its header sequence word, bounded by the session ACK limit
at handoff, and its exact Rwrite alone is custody; a Submitted naming it is
INVALID. Standalone acks answer BUSY while a folded commit is in flight;
EAGAIN keeps the word for the identical retry, any other reply drops it
unconfirmed. sf_validate accepts a nonzero word only on a FrameCommit. Open,
Close and paired submissions are unchanged. Spec copy of the wire contract
updated with the lean section; API-PARITY records the Rust comparison.
